# ThreadSpace - Claude Code Project Rules

## Project Overview
ThreadSpace is a community discussion platform (Reddit meets Discord) built with Next.js 14+ to demonstrate modern full-stack patterns.

## Tech Stack
- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4
- **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (new-york style)
- **Import Alias:** @/*

## Code Conventions

### Git Workflow
- **Main branch:** `develop` (not main)
- **Feature branches:** `feature/feature-name`
- **Commit messages:** Use conventional commits (feat:, fix:, chore:, refactor:, etc.)

### File Organization
```
src/
├── app/              # Next.js App Router
│   ├── (marketing)/ # Public pages (landing, about, blog)
│   └── (app)/       # Protected app pages (feed, communities)
├── components/      # Shared components
│   └── ui/         # shadcn/ui components
└── lib/            # Utilities and helpers
```

### Rendering Strategies
- **Static (SSG):** Marketing pages, documentation
- **ISR:** Community pages, blog posts (with revalidation)
- **SSR:** User dashboards, personalized content

### Component Guidelines
- Prefer Server Components by default
- Only use "use client" when needed (interactivity, hooks, browser APIs)
- Extract reusable UI into components
- Add aria-hidden to decorative SVGs

## Development Commands
```bash
npm run dev        # Start dev server
npm run build      # Production build
npm run lint       # Run ESLint
```

## Module Progress
